From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 01:16:52 -0400
Subject: look: Arc's rows, the page card, toasts, motion, the page-coloured
 row

The close glyph is laid out only while a row is hovered or focused and its
slot stays reserved; an essentials card keeps its favicon and shows an
audio alert as a corner badge (docs/features/tabs.md R1-R3, R18). Split
panes carry no ring, the link status bubble is a pill inside the card and
the find bar takes the dialog colours and the card's right edge
(docs/features/page.md). Screenshots raise a toast with Show in Finder, and
toasts take the window's colours (docs/features/screenshot.md C5-C7).
stedding::ShouldAnimate() gates every Stedding animation on macOS Reduce
Motion and a preference (docs/features/motion.md). The address row takes the
page's colour on either side of the contrast line and the toolbar's icons and
text flip for contrast through a supplier on the window's colour key
(docs/features/toolbar.md T4, T7); the card sits one gutter (6 DIP) from the
window's top, right and bottom edges, the row inside it.

Why: docs/ROUND6-PLAN.md wave 1 (R6-03, R6-05, R6-06, R6-07, R6-08) and the
operator's requests of 2026-09-05 (the page-coloured row, the equal gutter).
Removable when: Chromium's vertical tabs, status bubble, find bar and toasts
take these shapes upstream.
